{"verdict":"MAJOR","summary":"Evaluator contract, results-schema migration, and workflow-config allowlist are all under-specified; wrapper/runner boundary is ambiguous. Current TDD list mocks around the hardest unknowns.","issues_found":[{"severity":"MAJOR","area":"evaluator contract","detail":"Plan references 'evaluator registered for target_type' with no interface signature, return schema, registry location, or failure semantics. Tests mock evaluators, so the contract is never pinned. Real agent/template/workflow-config evaluators are undefined at v1, yet AC requires two non-skill target types."},{"severity":"MAJOR","area":"schema migration","detail":"Risks section admits downstream tooling may consume the skill-only results.tsv, but AC mandates replacing with target_type/target_path. Migration path (in-place vs additive JSONL) is left as an Open question while AC assumes it's decided — direct contradiction."},{"severity":"MAJOR","area":"workflow-config bounds","detail":"'Tight allowlist' is asserted as mitigation but no file path, format, ownership, or extension process is specified. Without a committed allowlist artifact the runner can silently broaden scope."},{"severity":"MAJOR","area":"wrapper/runner boundary","detail":"'Delegate existing skill flow into generic runner OR share its core logic' are different architectures. Branch isolation, main-branch protection, revert, and git_safe_commit currently live in shell; Python parity path isn't defined and new runner has no tests for those guarantees."}],"suggestions":[{"area":"evaluator","detail":"Pin a Protocol/TypedDict evaluator interface (score, warnings, criticals, diff_safety) and a registry module; require one real evaluator per declared v1 target type before acceptance."},{"area":"schema","detail":"Write an additive JSONL artifact beside results.tsv; forbid mutating the TSV until a downstream-consumer audit ships. Encode this in AC, not Open questions."},{"area":"allowlist","detail":"Commit config/autoresearch/workflow-config-allowlist.yaml with explicit paths; fail fast on non-listed targets; require PR review to extend."},{"area":"parity tests","detail":"Add Python-runner tests for branch naming, main-branch refusal, revert-on-regression, and git_safe_commit invocation — don't rely on the shell wrapper's existing suite."}],"questions_for_author":[{"q":"Does the Python runner reimplement branch/commit/revert or shell out to the existing script's functions?"},{"q":"Which concrete evaluator backs agent and template targets at v1, beyond mocked tests?"},{"q":"Is the results artifact additive or in-place, and when does the downstream-consumer audit land relative to this plan?"}]}
